{"repositoryId":1415154364,"availability":"available","full":"Ayesha-Ansa/research-evidence-analyst","name":"research-evidence-analyst","description":"An evidence-grounded RAG research assistant that combines semantic search, BM25 keyword retrieval, Reciprocal Rank Fusion, and cross-encoder reranking to answer questions from research papers with PDF page citations and evidence sufficiency checks.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":12,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-12T06:12:51Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:08:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://research-evidence-analyst-dtgmee6svlkqpbg6ctazqk.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.046Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.046Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.046Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.046Z","stars":12,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application for asking questions about research papers and PDF reports. It combines dense semantic search, BM25 keyword retrieval, Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF), and cross-encoder reranking to retrieve relevant passages before generating an evidence-grounded answer with source-page citations.","Research papers and technical reports can be long and difficult to search manually. This project provides a question-answering interface that retrieves passages from a selected document corpus, checks whether the retrieved evidence appears sufficient, and generates an answer grounded in that evidence. When the evidence is insufficient, the app is designed to abstain rather than confidently invent an answer.","Users can search either the included sample corpus or upload their own text-based PDF documents for the current app session."],"features":["Two corpus options: search the pre-indexed sample corpus or upload PDFs to create a temporary searchable corpus.","PDF processing: extract text page by page, split it into overlapping chunks, and preserve source filenames and page numbers.","Dense semantic retrieval: create embeddings for uploaded passages and search them with FAISS.","Keyword retrieval: use BM25 to retrieve passages based on lexical overlap.","Hybrid ranking: combine dense and BM25 rankings with Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ayesha-Ansa/research-evidence-analyst/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"62d63d51ec4468a21e37dbae656a8ed94d08e4a0c2db668085f574d2dc734ade","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.497Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.497Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interactive Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application for asking questions about research papers and PDF reports. It combines dense semantic search, BM25 keyword retrieval, Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF), and cross-encoder reranking to retrieve relevant passages before generating an evidence-grounded answer with source-page citations.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ayesha-Ansa/research-evidence-analyst/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"62d63d51ec4468a21e37dbae656a8ed94d08e4a0c2db668085f574d2dc734ade","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ayesha-Ansa/research-evidence-analyst/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.497Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T14:08:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ayesha-Ansa/research-evidence-analyst/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:08.498Z","hash":"62d63d51ec4468a21e37dbae656a8ed94d08e4a0c2db668085f574d2dc734ade","originalBytes":15203,"storedBytes":15203,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["retrieved","passages","api","key","corpus","evidence","retrieval","app","sample","answer","citation","streamlit","openai","pdf","pdfs","upload","page","search","source-page","relevant","project","question","source","uploaded","check","demo",